User Stories: Combat

As a developer, I want to be able to quickly generate an equation and solution of a given type so that I can use these throughout the game and have them be relatively unique (hard to memorize).

Priority: High, Estimate: 8 hours

Be able to generate a random single multiplication equation given the size of each factor (1h)
Be able to generate a random division equation (with or without remainder) given the size of the divisor and dividend (2h)
Be able to generate a random equation with multiple variables given the amount of variables and range of numbers (2h)
Write tests: for each equation type, test that the answer is correct for the given equation (1h)
Run Tests and Debug (2h)

As a player, I want to be able to fight and beat enemies by solving math equations so that I can progress through the levels of the game.

Priority: High, Estimate: 13 hours

Create a combat scene with player, enemy, and user interface, question popup (1h)
Connect interface elements to backend variables (2h)
Connect the combat scene to the question system, should be able to generate a question and verify the answer (2h)
Correct answers should damage the enemy and incorrect answers should have the enemy damage the player (2h)
If the player dies, show the game loss; If the enemy dies, show the level win (1h)
Write tests: damage on answer and health updates, win/loss detection, make sure health does not drop below zero, make sure all buttons work without ruining game flow (2h)
Run Tests and debug (3h)






As a player, I want to be able to use potions in battle instead of attacking so that I can heal during combat and not lose.

Priority: Medium, Estimate: 10 hours

Create buttons for option to attack or use potion during player turn (attack links to regular attack flow, potions leads to potion popup screen) (2h)
Create options to return to action select from attack question/potion use popups (1h)
Connect potion tracker and create visual way to see potions and click to use (2h)
If using a potion, should remove potion and heal player accordingly (then enemy attacks) (1h)
Write tests: Be able to move between actions without being attacked, make sure question for attack screen does not change after being seen, test that health stat updates accordingly, test that potion is removed from ‘inventory’ (2h)
Run Tests and Debug (2h)

User Stories: Rest
Enter Rest, as a player, I want to enter the rest page after a battle so that I can recover my health before the next battles.
Priority: High, Estimate: 8 hours
Create the Rest screen with an HP bar, recovery message, and Continue button (2h).
Connect the Rest screen to the combat system so players can enter after a battle (1h).
Restore the player's HP to maximum and update the health bar (2h).
Write tests: verify HP is fully restored, the health bar updates correctly, and the Continue button works (2h).
Run tests and fix bugs (1h).

In Rest, as a player, I want to see what mini games are available so that I can gain some bonuses before the next battle.
Priority: Low, Estimate: 8 hours
Create the Rest menu with Upgrade Mini Game, Potions Mini Game, and Leave Rest buttons (2h).
Connect the two minigame buttons to their corresponding screens (2h).
Connect the Leave Rest button to return the player to the main game (1h).
Write tests: verify all buttons navigate to the correct screens and the Rest menu displays correctly (2h).
Run tests and fix bugs (1h).




User Stories: Upgrade Minigame

As a player, I want to complete a math challenge to earn an upgrade, so that practicing math helps me strengthen my character.

Priority: High,  Estimate: 10 hours

Build the minigame screen with instructions, a math problem, and an answer field(1hr)
Display problems and check submitted answers (2hr)
Show feedback and allow another attempt after an incorrect answer (2hr)
Award a basic upgrade after a correct answer and display its effect (1hr).
Write tests for answer checking, invalid inputs, retries, and awarding the upgrade only once (2hr)
Run and debug (2 hours)

As a player, I want to choose which character stat to upgrade, so that I can improve my character to match my play style

Priority: High, Estimate: 10 hours

Build an upgrade selection screen showing weapon, defense, and potion options. (2hr)
Show each upgrade’s current stat and proposed increase (1hr)
Apply the selected upgrade after completing the math problems (2hr)
Update the character’s displayed stats and return to the game (1hr)
Write tests for all upgrade choices, correct stat increases, and preventing duplicate rewards (2hr)
Run and debug (2hr)

As a player, I want my earned upgrades to be saved, so that I keep my progress when I return to the game

Priority: Medium, Estimate: 8 hours

Save upgraded stats using the game’s progress storage system (2hr)
Restore saved upgrades when the player resumes the game (2hr)
Write tests for saving, restoring, and handling missing or invalid saved data (2hr)
Run and debug (2hr)


User Stories: Leaderboard

As a player, I want a way to keep track of all users’ scores so that I can get an idea of how my progress is relative to my peers.

Priority: Medium, Estimate: 8 hours

Set up backend to sync login system’s database and add score column to database so that we can read the scores of each player (1h)
Set up frontend to take all the usernames in the database and sort them in descending order of their scores (1h)
Set up UI for frontend which displays the list of usernames along with their scores and add appropriate colorings and formatting to make it look as close to the design as shown in the prototype [Did not show in prototype, but the leaderboard will be scrollable] (3h)
Add the Back button and set up the connection to go back to the previous page, and add the Leave button and set up the connection to go to the Title Screen (1h)
Write Tests: Usernames sorted in correct order based on scores, Correct usernames and scores are taken from the database, back and leave buttons work as intended (1h)
Run tests and debug (1h)

User Stories: Title Screen

As a player, I want to be able to log into my account so I can maintain progress of a previous game and track my high score.

Priority: Medium - Estimate: 10 hours

Create an interface that allows users to interact and enter sign in information. (1hr)
Create a database to hold user data and learn how to interact with it. The database will be able to hold usernames, passwords, high scores and game progress. (4h)
Send inputted user data to the database to be saved (1h)
Retrieve the correct user data based on the entered credentials (1h)
Load user data onto the player’s device (1h)
Test and debug (2h)

As a player, I want to be able to navigate from the title screen to gameplay or the leaderboard.

Priority: High - Estimate: 7 hours

Create an interface that allows the user to click on buttons to send them to different screens. (1h)
When the “New game” button is clicked, send user to combat screen (1h)
When the “Leaderboard” button is clicked, send user to the leaderboard screen (1h)
When the “Continue” button is clicked, interpret user data from the database to send the user to the appropriate screen (2h)
Test and debug (2h)


User Stories: Potion Lab
As a player, I want to solve an equation to brew a potion, so that I practice order of operations while preparing for fights.
Priority: High · Estimate: 10 hours
Generate or select an order-of-operations equation (2h)
Display the equation and an answer input field (2h)
Check whether the player's answer is correct (2h)
Write tests: verify equation display and correct/incorrect answer validation (2h)
Run tests and fix bugs (2h)

As a player, I want a correct answer to give me the potion, so that solving feels rewarding and helps me survive in upcoming fights.
Priority: High · Estimate: 7 hours
Connect a correct answer to successful potion brewing (2h)
Add the brewed potion to the player's inventory (1h)
Display a success message when the potion is obtained (1h)
Write tests: verify correct answers grant exactly one potion and update inventory correctly (2h)
Run tests and fix bugs (1h)


User Stories: Wrong Answer Explanation Popup

As a player, I want to see the correct answer when I answer a question incorrectly, so that I can recognize my mistake and learn from it. 
Priority: High · Estimate: 7 hours
Build the wrong answer popup with a display for the correct answer (2h)
Connect the popup to the question system so it appears after an incorrect answer (1h)
Display the correct answer for the specific question the student answered incorrectly (1h)
Write tests: popup appears after an incorrect answer and displays the correct answer for the current question (2h)
Run tests and debug (1h)

As a player, I want to see the step-by-step solution to a question I answered incorrectly, so that I can understand how to solve the problem correctly.
Priority: High · Estimate: 9 hours
Build a solution display for the wrong answer popup (2h)
Generate the correct solution steps for each supported question type (2h)
Display the solution steps in the correct order along with the final answer (2h)
Write tests: solution steps are correct, displayed in the correct order, and match the current question (2h)
Run tests and debug (1h)

As a teacher, I want students to receive accurate explanations and solutions, so that they can understand where they went wrong and how to fix their mistakes.
Priority: High · Estimate: 8 hours
Create accurate explanations for each supported question type (2h)
Connect explanations to the specific question and incorrect answer (2h)
Make sure the displayed answer, hints, and solution steps are mathematically correct (1h)
Write tests: explanations, answers, hints, and solution steps are accurate for each question type (2h)
Run tests and debug (1h)


